ush is non-fatal/tolerated and whether/how it is surfaced to the operator.","Both the per-fold push and the end-of-run safety-net push fail: the plan does not state the terminal disposition (stranded commits remain, deferred to next sync), leaving the fallback-chain winner unstated."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an inline disposition statement to Approach step 2: a failed per-fold push is non-fatal (logged, best-effort), the end-of-run _commit_backfill push retries it as the safety net, and if that also fails the commits remain local (recovered on the next sync.push) — no failure is swallowed.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a one-line positive rationale for choosing the timing hand-over over a fair/FIFO/queued-lock protocol (e.g. the store lock is cross-process and cross-host via the git-synced mkdir leg and is held by every write path, so a protocol-level fair lock has far larger blast radius than a scoped sweep-side pause), so the single chosen approach is anchored rather than merely constrained.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'The store lock is an unqueued polling lock.'","Plan step 1: the sweep 'stays off the lock for longer than the longest gap in which a waiter is not polling ... (about 0.6 s) ... (about 3 s)' and 'No new lock, env var, config key, or flag'","ABSENCE: no clause states WHY a fair/queued-lock protocol is rejected in favour of the cadence-tuned window (e.g. blast radius across every write path and the cross-host mkdir leg), only that no new lock will be added"],"finding":"The plan chooses a timing-based hand-over (a maintenance sweep sleeping a duration derived from the waiter's own poll/backoff cadence) over the structurally-different fair/FIFO/queued-lock approach that would eliminate the starvation root cause at the protocol level, but states only the bare constraint 'No new lock, env var, config key, or flag' without a positive rationale weighing the timing hand-over against making the lock fair. The chosen approach is defensible (a fair lock across a cross-process/cross-host git-synced store lock has large blast radius and touches every write path), so this is a missing-rationale gap, not a wrong-approach gap.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f49100831fbd77a84","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach, step 1 ('Hand the lock over before re-taking it'); Scope","norm_id":"n91f0724b894d15c6","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer or later maintainer questions whether the timing window is a durable fix versus making the lock fair, and the plan offers no recorded reasoning to settle it","Future poll/backoff-cadence changes tempt a re-open of the lock-protocol decision with no captured rationale to anchor against"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In Approach step 1, after 'No new lock, env var, config key, or flag', add: 'A protocol-level fair/queued lock would change the cross-process, cross-host (git-synced mkdir leg) store lock used by every write path; a sweep-side pause confines the change to the one starving producer, so it is preferred on blast radius and codebase alignment.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Justify the timed stand-aside heuristic against the established fair/FIFO/queued-lock prior art for polling-lock writer starvation: state why a protocol-level fair lock is rejected and why a cadence-tuned hand-over window is an acceptable (and durable) substitute, or adopt the fair-lock approach.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'The store lock is an unqueued polling lock.' and 'No new lock, env var, config key, or flag'","Plan Approach 1: the sweep 'stays off the lock for longer than the longest gap in which a waiter is not polling... (about 0.6 s)... (about 3 s)' — a timing heuristic tuned to the waiter's poll cadence, not a hand-off guarantee","Retrieved prior art (DuckDuckGo, this run): Atlas 'Spinlock...' — 'Ticket locks and queue-based locks improve fairness by controlling acquisition order... A spinlock without fairness can starve a task under repeated reacquisition'; systemoverflow 'Fair/FIFO: no starvation, strict ordering'; systemoverflow 'Fair locks: Use locks with FIFO acquisition order'; LKML 'Implement Batched (group) ticket lock' (FIFO fairness)","ABSENCE: no section of the plan names FIFO/queued/ticket locking as the alternative it is choosing against, nor explains why a tuned stand-aside beats making the lock fair"],"finding":"The plan adopts a novel lock-fairness pattern — a maintenance sweep that sleeps a duration computed from the waiting writer's own poll/backoff cadence to engineer a window where the waiter wins — on an explicitly unqueued polling lock, without considering the dominant prior art for this exact failure mode (fair/FIFO/queued 'ticket' locks that build acquisition-order fairness into the lock protocol). The plan explicitly rejects that approach ('No new lock...') but never weighs the timing heuristic against it, so the novelty is unjustified under anti-repackaging / Rule-of-Three.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f487db440b154a863","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Root cause + Approach step 1; scope note 'The store lock is an unqueued polling lock'","norm_id":"nf9a4861c00dd0862","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future writer with a poll cadence or backoff different from today's (or a reviewer later adding a new acquire() caller with a non-default timeout) silently falls outside the hand-over window the constants were tuned for, and the starvation returns — the very fragility a fair/queued lock would not have","A reviewer asks 'why not just make the lock fair?' and the plan has no recorded answer"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a short 'Prior art / alternatives' note to the Approach or Root-cause section: cite that FIFO/ticket/queued locks are the standard remedy for unfair-polling-lock starvation, explain the concrete reason to avoid one here (e.g., cross-host advisory lock over a git store cannot cheaply maintain a shared wait queue, and the existing two-leg fcntl+mkdir protocol has no queue), and note the heuristic's dependence on the shared poll-cadence constants (already addressed by deriving the gap from those same constants via max_waiter_gap_s). Explicitly flag that any new acquire() caller using a sub-1s or non-whole-second timeout, or a change to the poll/backoff cadence, must be re-checked against the hand-over window.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"983a1b4959f64895","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["f82923713354da13",6395],"description_boxes":["0aad7da77d2ed59c",0],"file_impact":["8c7bc1e869efc206",3],"ticket_id":["7099fbc28ba7a65b",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":669845,"cache_write_tokens":181018,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":10973.3,"input_tokens":874751,"llm_calls":28,"